      "subject": "Communications & Information Theory",
      "subjectSlug": "communications",
      "topic": "Amplitude & Frequency Modulation (AM, FM)",
      "type": "NAT",
      "question": "<p>An AM broadcast signal has a carrier power $P_c = 10\\text{ kW}$ and modulation index $\\mu = 0.8$. The total transmitted power $P_t = P_c \\left(1 + \\frac{\\mu^2}{2}\\right)$ (in $\\text{kW}$) is ________.</p>",
      "options": [],
      "structuredOptions": [],
      "answer": [
        "13.2"
      ],
      "tolerance": {
        "min": 13.0,
        "max": 13.4
      },
      "marks": 2,
      "negativeMarks": 0,
      "explanation": "<div class='space-y-2'><p><strong>Step-by-Step Solution (Communications & Information Theory):</strong></p><p>$P_t = 10 \\left(1 + \\frac{0.8^2}{2}\\right) = 10 \\left(1 + \\frac{0.64}{2}\\right) = 10(1 + 0.32) = 13.2\\text{ kW}$.</p></div>"
    },
    {
      "id": "gate-ec-comm-q2",
