      "year": 2024,
      "orderIndex": 2,
      "section": "EC",
      "title": "GATE EC — Comm Systems | Information Theory & Channel Capacity",
      "subject": "Communications & Information Theory",
      "subjectSlug": "communications",
      "topic": "Information Theory & Channel Capacity",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "question": "<p>According to Shannon's Channel Capacity theorem, the capacity $C$ of an additive white Gaussian noise (AWGN) channel with bandwidth $B$ and signal-to-noise ratio $\\text{SNR} = S/N$ is:</p>",
      "options": [
        "$C = B \\log_2 \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$",
        "$C = 2 B \\log_2 \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$",
        "$C = B \\log_{10} \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$",
        "$C = B \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$"
      ],
      "structuredOptions": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "$C = B \\log_2 \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$",
          "html": "$C = B \\log_2 \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "$C = 2 B \\log_2 \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$",
          "html": "$C = 2 B \\log_2 \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "$C = B \\log_{10} \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$",
          "html": "$C = B \\log_{10} \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "$C = B \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$",
          "html": "$C = B \\left(1 + \\frac{S}{N}\\right)$"
        }
      ],
      "answer": [
        "A"
      ],
      "tolerance": null,
      "marks": 2,
      "negativeMarks": 0.67,
      "explanation": "<div class='space-y-2'><p><strong>Step-by-Step Solution (Communications & Information Theory):</strong></p><p>Shannon-Hartley theorem states maximum error-free transmission capacity is $C = B \\log_2 (1 + \\text{SNR})$ bits/second.</p></div>"
